          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-001",
              "name": "S3 bucket without server-side encryption",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "S3 bucket without server-side encryption"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "S3 buckets should encrypt objects at rest. A bucket with no server_side_encryption_configuration block relies on the account default, which may not exist. Standalone aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption_configuration resources are acknowledged but require graph correlation to attribute.\n\nHow to fix:\nAdd a server_side_encryption_configuration block:\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption_configuration\" \"this\" {\n  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.this.id\n  rule {\n    apply_server_side_encryption_by_default {\n      sse_algorithm = \"AES256\"  # or \"aws:kms\" with kms_master_key_id\n    }\n    bucket_key_enabled = true\n  }\n}"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/bucket-encryption.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-002",
              "name": "S3 bucket with public ACL",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "S3 bucket with public ACL"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Bucket ACLs granting public-read, public-read-write, or authenticated-read expose objects beyond the account.\n\nHow to fix:\nRemove the public ACL grant. Set the bucket ACL to private and rely on bucket\npolicies for access control:\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_acl\" \"this\" {\n  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.this.id\n  acl    = \"private\"\n}\nThen enable all four public-access-block settings (see AEGIS-AWS-003 fix)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/acl-overview.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-003",
              "name": "S3 bucket policy allows public principal",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "S3 bucket policy allows public principal"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An Allow statement with Principal \"*\" grants anonymous access to the bucket, bypassing ACL controls.\n\nHow to fix:\nRemove the public principal from the bucket policy. Replace\n`\"Principal\": \"*\"` with specific IAM ARNs, or delete the policy statement entirely if public access was unintentional. Then enable all four\npublic-access-block settings:\nresource \"aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block\" \"this\" {\n  bucket                  = aws_s3_bucket.this.id\n  block_public_acls       = true\n  block_public_policy     = true\n  ignore_public_acls      = true\n  restrict_public_buckets = true\n}"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-control-block-public-access.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "critical"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-004",
              "name": "Security group ingress open to the world",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Security group ingress open to the world"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Ingress rules allowing 0.0.0.0/0 expose the workload to the entire internet. Restrict source CIDRs to known ranges.\n\nHow to fix:\nRestrict the ingress CIDR to trusted ranges. Replace `0.0.0.0/0` with your\noffice/VPN CIDRs, or remove the rule and use SSM Session Manager (no inbound\nSSH needed):\ningress {\n  from_port   = 22\n  to_port     = 22\n  protocol    = \"tcp\"\n  cidr_blocks = [\"203.0.113.0/24\"]  # your trusted range\n}"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-security-groups.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-005",
              "name": "Security group egress open to the world",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Security group egress open to the world"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Egress rules allowing 0.0.0.0/0 permit unrestricted outbound traffic, aiding data exfiltration. Restrict destinations to required ranges.\n\nHow to fix:\nRemove public exposure. Restrict ingress to known CIDR ranges, move the resource into private subnets, and front it with a load balancer or API gateway if external access is required. Verify with `aws ec2 describe-security-groups`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-security-groups.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-006",
              "name": "IAM policy allows all actions on all resources",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "IAM policy allows all actions on all resources"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An Allow statement with Action \"*\" on Resource \"*\" is administrative access. Scope actions and resources to least privilege.\n\nHow to fix:\nReplace the wildcard policy with least-privilege statements. List only the\nactions the workload needs on only the ARNs it touches:\npolicy = jsonencode({\n  Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n  Statement = [{\n    Effect   = \"Allow\"\n    Action   = [\"s3:GetObject\", \"s3:PutObject\"]\n    Resource = [\"arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket/*\"]\n  }]\n})\nUse IAM Access Analyzer policy generation from CloudTrail to derive the minimum set."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html#grant-least-privilege",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "critical"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-007",
              "name": "RDS instance without storage encryption",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "RDS instance without storage encryption"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "RDS storage should be encrypted at rest. The provider default for storage_encrypted is false, so an absent attribute is a finding.\n\nHow to fix:\nEnable storage encryption on the RDS instance:\nresource \"aws_db_instance\" \"this\" {\n  # ...\n  storage_encrypted = true\n  kms_key_id        = aws_kms_key.rds.arn  # optional CMK\n}\nNote: encryption cannot be enabled on an existing unencrypted instance —\ntake a snapshot, copy it with encryption, and restore."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/Overview.Encryption.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-008",
              "name": "RDS instance without deletion protection",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "RDS instance without deletion protection"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Deletion protection guards against accidental database destruction. The provider default is false.\n\nHow to fix:\nEnable deletion protection to prevent accidental destruction:\nresource \"aws_db_instance\" \"this\" {\n  deletion_protection = true\n}\nFor S3, remove `force_destroy = true`. For EC2, set `disable_api_termination = true`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_DeleteInstance.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-009",
              "name": "EBS volume without encryption",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "EBS volume without encryption"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "EBS volumes should be encrypted at rest. The provider default for encrypted is false, so an absent attribute is a finding.\n\nHow to fix:\nEnable encryption at rest. For AWS-managed keys add the service's encryption block (e.g. `storage_encrypted = true` for RDS, `server_side_encryption_configuration` for S3). For regulated data use a customer-managed KMS key via `kms_key_id` and enable key rotation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-010",
              "name": "CloudTrail without log file validation",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CloudTrail without log file validation"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Log file validation detects tampering with CloudTrail logs after delivery. The provider default for enable_log_file_validation is false, so an absent attribute is a finding.\n\nHow to fix:\nEnable audit logging. Turn on CloudTrail (multi-region, log file validation, KMS-encrypted bucket), VPC flow logs, and service access logs. Ship logs to a dedicated, MFA-delete-protected bucket in a security account."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-user-guide.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-011",
              "name": "RDS instance publicly accessible",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "RDS instance publicly accessible"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A publicly accessible database accepts connections from the internet. Keep databases in private subnets with publicly_accessible false (the provider default).\n\nHow to fix:\nSet `publicly_accessible = false` and move the database to private subnets:\nresource \"aws_db_instance\" \"this\" {\n  # ...\n  publicly_accessible = false\n  db_subnet_group_name = aws_db_subnet_group.private.name\n}\nAccess the database via a bastion host, VPN, or SSM port forwarding — never directly."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_VPC.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-012",
              "name": "S3 bucket without versioning",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "S3 bucket without versioning"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Versioning protects against accidental deletion and overwrites and is required for reliable recovery. Provider default is disabled.\n\nHow to fix:\nEnable data protection. Turn on versioning / point-in-time recovery / automated backups with a retention period ≥ 7 days (30+ for production). Test restores regularly — untested backups are not backups."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/whatisbackup.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-101",
              "name": "IAM role assumable by anyone",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "IAM role assumable by anyone"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An Allow statement in the trust policy with Principal \"*\" lets any AWS identity assume this role. Restrict the principal to specific accounts, roles, or services.\n\nHow to fix:\nLock down the role trust policy. Replace the wildcard principal with the\nspecific IAM ARNs or federated providers allowed to assume the role, and add\na condition such as `aws:PrincipalOrgID` or `sts:ExternalId`:\nassume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n  Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n  Statement = [{\n    Effect    = \"Allow\"\n    Principal = { AWS = \"arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/DeployRole\" }\n    Action    = \"sts:AssumeRole\"\n    Condition = { StringEquals = { \"sts:ExternalId\" = \"unique-value\" } }\n  }]\n})"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_terms-and-concepts.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "critical"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-102",
              "name": "IAM managed policy grants administrative access",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "IAM managed policy grants administrative access"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An Allow statement with Action \"*\" (or \"iam:*\") on Resource \"*\" is administrative access in a customer-managed policy. Scope actions and resources to least privilege.\n\nHow to fix:\nReplace the admin-managed policy attachment with scoped inline or customer-managed\npolicies (see AEGIS-AWS-006 fix). If break-glass admin access is required, gate it\nbehind a separate role with MFA condition and CloudTrail alerting:\nCondition = { Bool = { \"aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent\" = \"true\" } }"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html#grant-least-privilege",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-104",
              "name": "Public S3 exfiltration path",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Public S3 exfiltration path"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An S3 bucket is readable by the public internet through a bucket policy granting s3:GetObject to everyone, or a public ACL: a complete path exists from the internet to the bucket's data.\n\nHow to fix:\nBreak the public exfiltration path. Make the S3 bucket private (see AEGIS-AWS-003\nfix), remove the overly permissive IAM policy (see AEGIS-AWS-006 fix), and\nensure the compute role cannot reach public buckets. Treat this as an active\nincident path: audit CloudTrail for `s3:GetObject` calls from the affected role."
              },
