              "name": "Multi-hop network attack path to database",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Multi-hop network attack path to database"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A database is reachable from the internet through a chain of hops — e.g. a world-open security group leading to a second security group, or a compromised EC2 stepping stone sharing the database's security group. No single hop looks critical alone.\n\nHow to fix:\nReview the flagged configuration against AWS security best practices and the CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark. Apply the control the rule describes, preferring restrictive defaults, encryption, and audit logging. Validate with `aegis scan` after the change."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-standards.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "high"
