            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-202",
              "name": "Load balancer listener uses plain HTTP",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Load balancer listener uses plain HTTP"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A listener terminating plain HTTP sends credentials and session tokens in cleartext. Listeners should use HTTPS (or TLS) with a certificate.\n\nHow to fix:\nReplace the HTTP listener with HTTPS. Create an ACM certificate and attach it:\nresource \"aws_lb_listener\" \"https\" {\n  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.this.arn\n  port              = 443\n  protocol          = \"HTTPS\"\n  ssl_policy        = \"ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06\"\n  certificate_arn   = aws_acm_certificate.this.arn\n  default_action { type = \"forward\" target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.this.arn }\n}\nAdd an HTTP listener that redirects to HTTPS (301)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/create-https-listener.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "critical"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-203",
              "name": "Load balancer not dropping invalid headers",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Load balancer not dropping invalid headers"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Without drop_invalid_header_fields, malformed HTTP headers reach targets and enable request-smuggling style attacks. The provider default is false.\n\nHow to fix:\nReview the flagged configuration against AWS security best practices and the CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark. Apply the control the rule describes, preferring restrictive defaults, encryption, and audit logging. Validate with `aegis scan` after the change."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-standards.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "high"
