            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-205",
              "name": "Subnet auto-assigns public IPs",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Subnet auto-assigns public IPs"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "map_public_ip_on_launch = true gives every instance in the subnet a public address by default, bypassing the intended private-subnet design.\n\nHow to fix:\nRemove public exposure. Restrict ingress to known CIDR ranges, move the resource into private subnets, and front it with a load balancer or API gateway if external access is required. Verify with `aws ec2 describe-security-groups`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-security-groups.html",
