              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A block_device_mappings entry in an aws_launch_template whose ebs map has encrypted = false leaves the volume readable at rest. (Known false only; absent follows the provider default.)\n\nHow to fix:\nEnable encryption at rest. For AWS-managed keys add the service's encryption block (e.g. `storage_encrypted = true` for RDS, `server_side_encryption_configuration` for S3). For regulated data use a customer-managed KMS key via `kms_key_id` and enable key rotation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html",
