              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An aws_api_gateway_stage without client_certificate_id cannot present a client certificate to backend integrations, so backends cannot authenticate that calls genuinely come from API Gateway. Generate a client certificate and attach it to the stage when the backend supports mutual authentication.\n\nHow to fix:\nReview the flagged configuration against AWS security best practices and the CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark. Apply the control the rule describes, preferring restrictive defaults, encryption, and audit logging. Validate with `aegis scan` after the change."
