              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A KMS key with deletion_window_in_days below the 30-day default leaves almost no time to notice and cancel an accidental or malicious key deletion.\n\nHow to fix:\nEnable encryption at rest. For AWS-managed keys add the service's encryption block (e.g. `storage_encrypted = true` for RDS, `server_side_encryption_configuration` for S3). For regulated data use a customer-managed KMS key via `kms_key_id` and enable key rotation."
