              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An OpenSearch domain with no log_publishing_options block sends no audit, slow-query or error logs to CloudWatch, blinding incident response. Publish AUDIT_LOGS (and slow logs) to CloudWatch Logs.\n\nHow to fix:\nEnable audit logging. Turn on CloudTrail (multi-region, log file validation, KMS-encrypted bucket), VPC flow logs, and service access logs. Ship logs to a dedicated, MFA-delete-protected bucket in a security account."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-user-guide.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-814",
              "name": "Neptune cluster not copying tags to snapshots",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Neptune cluster not copying tags to snapshots"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A Neptune cluster with copy_tags_to_snapshot = false (the default) produces untagged snapshots, breaking cost allocation and data-classification tagging on backups. Set copy_tags_to_snapshot = true.\n\nHow to fix:\nEnable data protection. Turn on versioning / point-in-time recovery / automated backups with a retention period ≥ 7 days (30+ for production). Test restores regularly — untested backups are not backups."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/whatisbackup.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "low"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-820",
              "name": "Athena workgroup without SSE-KMS query result encryption",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Athena workgroup without SSE-KMS query result encryption"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "An Athena workgroup whose result encryption_option is not SSE_KMS (SSE_S3 or CSE_KMS are the common gaps) stores query results in S3 without a customer managed key, forfeiting key-policy control over potentially sensitive result sets. Use SSE_KMS with a customer managed key.\n\nHow to fix:\nEnable encryption at rest. For AWS-managed keys add the service's encryption block (e.g. `storage_encrypted = true` for RDS, `server_side_encryption_configuration` for S3). For regulated data use a customer-managed KMS key via `kms_key_id` and enable key rotation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-826",
              "name": "CloudFront distribution without a response headers policy",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CloudFront distribution without a response headers policy"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A CloudFront distribution with no response_headers_policy_id serves responses without hardened security headers (HSTS, frame-options, content-type options). Attach a response headers policy such as the managed SecurityHeadersPolicy.\n\nHow to fix:\nApply least privilege. Replace wildcard (`*`) actions and resources with the minimum scoped ARNs the workload needs. Split policy authoring from attachment. Use IAM Access Analyzer to generate scoped policies from CloudTrail history."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "low"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-836",
              "name": "Backup vault without vault lock configuration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Backup vault without vault lock configuration"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A Backup vault with no aws_backup_vault_lock_configuration allows recovery points to be deleted before their retention period expires, undermining ransomware protection. Add a vault lock in compliance mode with a minimum retention.\n\nHow to fix:\nEnable data protection. Turn on versioning / point-in-time recovery / automated backups with a retention period ≥ 7 days (30+ for production). Test restores regularly — untested backups are not backups."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/whatisbackup.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "low"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-AWS-840",
              "name": "Load balancer target group using plaintext HTTP",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Load balancer target group using plaintext HTTP"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A load balancer target group with protocol = \"HTTP\" forwards traffic to targets unencrypted inside the VPC, exposing request data and credentials to network sniffing. Use HTTPS with valid target certificates.\n\nHow to fix:\nEnforce TLS 1.2+. Replace HTTP listeners with HTTPS, set a modern TLS policy (e.g. `ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06`), and redirect HTTP→HTTPS. Disable weak ciphers and old protocol versions everywhere."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/classic/elb-security-policy-table.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "medium"
              }
