            {
              "id": "AEGIS-K8S-001",
              "name": "Container running as privileged",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Container running as privileged"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A privileged container has full access to the host, bypassing almost all isolation. Privilege is almost never required for application containers.\n\nHow to fix:\nDrop privileged mode. Remove `securityContext.privileged: true` and use the\nminimum Linux capabilities the container needs:\nsecurityContext:\n  allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n  runAsNonRoot: true\n  capabilities:\n    drop: [\"ALL\"]\nEnforce with Pod Security Standards (restricted) or Kyverno/OPA policies."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/security/pod-security-standards/",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "critical"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-K8S-002",
              "name": "Container running as root user",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Container running as root user"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Containers should run as a non-root user. An explicit runAsNonRoot: false or runAsUser: 0 keeps the container root, magnifying the impact of a container escape.\n\nHow to fix:\nEnable MFA on the account and restrict root usage. Create individual IAM users or federate via SSO, attach least-privilege policies, and never use root for daily operations."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_root-user.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-K8S-006",
              "name": "Container without resource limits",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Container without resource limits"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A container without resources.limits for cpu and memory can exhaust node resources (noisy neighbor / DoS). Set cpu and memory limits on every container.\n\nHow to fix:\nReview the flagged configuration against AWS security best practices and the CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark. Apply the control the rule describes, preferring restrictive defaults, encryption, and audit logging. Validate with `aegis scan` after the change."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-standards.html",
