              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Pod with hostNetwork enabled"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A pod with hostNetwork: true shares the node's network namespace, bypassing network policies and exposing host ports. Avoid hostNetwork.\n\nHow to fix:\nReview the flagged configuration against AWS security best practices and the CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark. Apply the control the rule describes, preferring restrictive defaults, encryption, and audit logging. Validate with `aegis scan` after the change."
