            {
              "id": "AEGIS-SC-005",
              "name": "Provisioner executes remote commands",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Provisioner executes remote commands"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A provisioner block with an 'inline' command list executes arbitrary commands on the remote host during apply (the remote-exec pattern). Provisioners are a last resort: they run outside the declarative model, often with elevated privileges, and their failures leave infrastructure half-configured. Prefer user_data, configuration management, or immutable images.\n\nHow to fix:\nReview the flagged configuration against AWS security best practices and the CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark. Apply the control the rule describes, preferring restrictive defaults, encryption, and audit logging. Validate with `aegis scan` after the change."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-standards.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-TF-004",
              "name": "Terraform CLI version not pinned",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Terraform CLI version not pinned"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Without terraform.required_version, any CLI version may run this configuration; behavior and provider-protocol differences across versions can change what gets applied.\n\nHow to fix:\nReview the flagged configuration against AWS security best practices and the CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark. Apply the control the rule describes, preferring restrictive defaults, encryption, and audit logging. Validate with `aegis scan` after the change."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-standards.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "medium"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-TF-005",
              "name": "Terraform backend using plaintext HTTP",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Terraform backend using plaintext HTTP"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "A backend address over http:// sends the state file — including secrets — in cleartext on the network.\n\nHow to fix:\nEnforce TLS 1.2+. Replace HTTP listeners with HTTPS, set a modern TLS policy (e.g. `ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06`), and redirect HTTP→HTTPS. Disable weak ciphers and old protocol versions everywhere."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/classic/elb-security-policy-table.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "high"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "AEGIS-TF-007",
              "name": "Terraform configuration without required_providers",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Terraform configuration without required_providers"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Without a required_providers block, provider sources and versions are implicit; Terraform may select unexpected providers or versions.\n\nHow to fix:\nReview the flagged configuration against AWS security best practices and the CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark. Apply the control the rule describes, preferring restrictive defaults, encryption, and audit logging. Validate with `aegis scan` after the change."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/securityhub-standards.html",
              "properties": {
                "severity": "low"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
